.DS_Store
/target
Cargo.lock
# NB: tools/gasp-emit/Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT force-tracked. Cargo
# regenerates it on every build (harness's and the agent's own), which made it
# a tracked-but-dirty file that `git add -A` swept into evolve commits and the
# protected-file guard then reverted — killing every real src/ commit. Ignoring
# it (like the root Cargo.lock) keeps it out of the sweep so commits land.
